Instead of this retry logic, would it make sense to just do the EVP_CIPHER_fetch, and return that value if its not null?  If it is NULL, then walk through the OBJ_to_name translation?  i.e.:

```
const EVP_CIPHER *evp_get_cipherbyname_ex(OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx,
                                          const char *name)
{
     EVP_CIPHER *cp = EVP_CIPHER_fetch(libctx, name, NULL);
     if (cp != NULL)
          return cp;
     cp = (const EVP_CIPHER *)OBJ_NAME_get(name, OBJ_NAME_TYPE_CIPHER_METH);
     ....
```

That seems like it would be more compact and performant
